\section{Summary}

This evaluation strategy provides a comprehensive framework for measuring the CCRMS framework's performance, usability, and economic viability. The 13 evaluation scenarios cover all six research objectives, while the mixed-methods data collection strategy ensures both rigorous quantitative measurement and rich qualitative insight.

\textbf{Key Deliverables from Evaluation:}
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Performance metrics across all KPI categories
    \item Comparative analysis against Ethereum L2 and centralised alternatives
    \item Feasibility assessment for ZK proof integration
    \item Monte-Carlo simulation results for creator savings
    \item Usability scores and user feedback synthesis
    \item Expert validation of architectural decisions
\end{enumerate}

The measurement-focused approach ensures that regardless of specific outcomes, the evaluation produces meaningful academic contribution through documented findings, comparative analysis, and actionable recommendations.

\textit{This document satisfies the Phase 2 Week 9--10 deliverable: ``Design evaluation scenarios and data collection strategy.'' It is prepared for integration into the thesis Methodology and Evaluation chapters.}

